# Portfolio Website Project

This is a cloud engineer portfolio website with:
- React frontend (Vite build system)
- Terraform infrastructure for AWS (S3 + CloudFront + Route53 + ACM)
- Docker-based Terraform runner

## Project Structure

```
src/App.jsx          - Main React component with CONFIG and SCRIPTS to customize
terraform/           - AWS infrastructure as code
terraform/bootstrap/ - State backend setup (run first)
run.sh              - Docker commands for Terraform operations
```

## Key Files to Edit

1. `src/App.jsx` - Update CONFIG object with user's details:
   - name, title, github username
   - email, linkedin
   - yearsExperience
   - certifications array
   - skills object

2. `src/App.jsx` - Update SCRIPTS object with user's scripts:
   - powershell array
   - bash array  
   - terraform array

3. `terraform/terraform.tfvars` - Set domain_name for deployment

## Development Commands

```bash
npm install          # Install dependencies
npm run dev          # Start dev server at localhost:5173
npm run build        # Production build to dist/
```

## Deployment Commands (requires Docker)

```bash
./run.sh bootstrap-init   # Initialize state backend
./run.sh bootstrap-apply  # Create S3 + DynamoDB for state
./run.sh init             # Initialize main Terraform
./run.sh plan             # Preview infrastructure changes
./run.sh apply            # Deploy infrastructure
./run.sh build            # Build React app in Docker
./run.sh deploy           # Sync to S3 + invalidate CloudFront
```

## Tech Stack

- React 18 + Vite
- Tailwind-style CSS (custom properties)
- JetBrains Mono + Space Grotesk fonts
- Terraform 1.7+
- AWS: S3, CloudFront, Route53, ACM, DynamoDB

## Solution Diagram Guidelines

When creating or modifying architecture diagrams in the Solutions page:

### Icon Standards
- Use official AWS icons from `/public/aws-icons/` folder
- Available icons: `s3.svg`, `cloudfront.svg`, `acm.svg`, `ec2.svg`, `elb.svg`, `rds.svg`, `waf.svg`, `autoscaling.svg`, `cloudflare.svg`
- Icons should be 20-36px depending on component size
- Use `<image href="/aws-icons/{service}.svg">` in SVG diagrams

### Layout Consistency
- Service boxes: rounded rectangles with 2px stroke
- Icon positioned at top-left of service box
- Service name below icon, centered
- Use monospace font (fontFamily="monospace")
- Text should not overlap with connection lines
- Flow labels should have background boxes for readability

### Color Scheme
- CloudFlare: #F6821F (orange)
- CloudFront: #8B5CF6 (purple)
- S3: #7AA116 (green)
- ACM: #DD344C (red)
- EC2: #FF9900 (orange)
- RDS: #3B48CC (blue)
- ELB: #8B5CF6 (purple)
- WAF: #DD344C (red)
- VPC border: #8B5CF6 (purple)
- AWS Cloud border: #FF9900 (orange, dashed)

### Connection Lines
- Use arrows with markers for direction
- Label connections above the line, not overlapping
- Use service-appropriate colors for arrows
